  <static seed="130" source="Library/PCC/BasicAlgebra/Exponents/negExp36.pg">
    <statement><p>Simplify the following expression, and write your answer using only <em>positive</em> exponents.</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle\frac{-5y^{44}}{9y^{46}}=</m><fillin characters="12" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p>Note that you may have to be careful with grouping parenthesis in this problem; 1/2y
is not the same as 1/(2y).</p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{-5}{9y^{2}}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p>We use the properties of exponents to help us here, remembering that <m>\displaystyle{\frac{a^m}{a^n} = a^{m-n}}</m></p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{           \begin{aligned}
                 \displaystyle\frac{-5y^{44}}{9y^{46}} \amp = \frac{-5}{9}y^{44-46}\\
                                                       \amp  =\frac{-5}{9}y^{-2}\\
                                    \amp  = -\frac{5}{9 y^{2}}
           \end{aligned}
    }</m></p>
</solution>
